+/* ZyperOS (yabasanshiro-atlas.patch): the texture atlas lives in the CPU's
+ * own memory and goes up with glTexSubImage2D from there, with no pixel
+ * buffer bound. It was a pixel buffer, mapped for the CPU to fill and
+ * uploaded from with the buffer bound; on Panfrost that upload read the
+ * buffer back from uncached memory on the CPU: 15.3 ms of Virtua Fighter
+ * 2's 54 ms frame on the GKD Pixel 2, 5.1 ms from the CPU's memory
+ * (2026-11-20). The atlas is filled again every frame, so nothing else
+ * reads it. */
